# LyricFren Project Guidelines

## Tech Stack

### Frontend
- Vue 3 (with Composition API)
- TailwindCSS v4
- PrimeVue v4
- OpenAPI JS client for AI integration

### Backend
- Express.js server
- Local document-oriented database (options to discuss)
  - Potential options: PouchDB, LowDB, SQLite with JSON support

## Architecture

- SPA frontend with RESTful API communication to backend
- Component-based UI architecture
- Local-first approach for data storage
- AI integration via OpenAPI

## Code Style & Conventions

- Use Vue SFCs with `<script setup>` syntax
- Follow Vue 3 Composition API patterns
- Use PrimeVue components for complex UI elements
- Implement responsive design with Tailwind utility classes

## Project Structure

- `/src` - Vue frontend code
  - `/components` - Reusable Vue components
  - `/views` - Page components
  - `/services` - API clients and services
  - `/stores` - State management
  - `/types` - TypeScript type definitions
- `/server` - Express backend
  - `/routes` - API endpoints
  - `/controllers` - Business logic
  - `/models` - Data models
  - `/db` - Database configuration

## Database Considerations

For local JSON document storage, consider:
- PouchDB: Syncs with CouchDB, good for offline-first
- LowDB: Simple JSON database with good performance
- SQLite: More structured but with JSON column support
- NeDB: MongoDB-like API but stores data locally
